<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Topic//EN" "topic.dtd">
<topic id="http-openapi">
  <title>Create a user from the API description</title>
  <body>
    <data name="doc-detective" value='test {"testId":"http-openapi","detectSteps":true,"openApi":[{"name":"users","descriptionPath":"users.openapi.json","validateAgainstSchema":"both","headers":"X-Test: docs"}]}'/>
    <p>The Users API description, <codeph>users.openapi.json</codeph>, defines each operation with an example.</p>
    <p>Call the <codeph>createUser</codeph> operation with its example request. The response matches the example user, Ada.</p>
    <data name="doc-detective" value='step {"httpRequest":{"openApi":{"name":"users","operationId":"createUser","headers":{"X-Request-Source":"docs"},"useExample":"both","server":"http://localhost:8093/api","statusCode":200}}}'/>
    <p>Call <codeph>createUser</codeph> again with your own user. The response includes the <codeph>name</codeph> and <codeph>job</codeph> fields.</p>
    <data name="doc-detective" value='step {"httpRequest":{"openApi":"createUser","request":{"body":{"name":"Grace","job":"admiral"}},"response":{"body":{"name":"Grace"},"required":["name","job"]}}}'/>
    <p>The <codeph>getUser</codeph> operation isn't live yet, so preview its response from the description's <codeph>ada</codeph> example.</p>
    <data name="doc-detective" value='step {"httpRequest":{"openApi":{"operationId":"getUser","mockResponse":true,"useExample":"response","exampleKey":"ada","validateAgainstSchema":"response"},"response":{"body":{"name":"Ada"}}}}'/>
    <data name="doc-detective" value="test end"/>
  </body>
</topic>
